LEAKYLEFT PUBLIC LICENSE
Version 0.0.0 — Too Late

THIS IS A FICTIONAL LICENSE AND A WORK OF SATIRE.
NO LEGAL FORCE OR ENFORCEABLE OBLIGATIONS ARE CLAIMED.

This is an original parody of licensing and compliance rituals. It is separate
from GNU GPL and is not affiliated with the GNU Project or the Free Software
Foundation. The provisions below describe an imaginary regime. They are not
intended to license real software or personal data, grant rights in anyone's
information, establish consent, or replace privacy protections.

PREAMBLE

The information has already left the building. The building has issued a
statement explaining how seriously it takes doors.

Leakyleft proposes the obvious next step: attach terms to the copies and hope
that accountability spreads as efficiently as the spreadsheet did.

Where ordinary copyleft asks what must accompany a copy, Leakyleft asks who
authorized the export, why the folder was public, and whether the apology is
available in an editable format.

The following provisions apply only inside this fiction.

0. DEFINITIONS

"Source Person" means the imaginary human whose life was converted into a row
in somebody else's growth strategy.

"Covered Fiction" means wholly invented records expressly presented as part
of this satire. No real person's information is covered by this document.

"Downstream Recipient" means anyone who receives a copy and immediately makes
another copy for safekeeping.

"Compliance" means the condition in which the paperwork is complete and the
problem is still present.

1. THE CHAIN OF REGRET

Every redistribution of Covered Fiction must preserve this notice and append
a full account of the decisions that made the previous redistribution seem
like a good idea.

These accounts must travel with all subsequent copies. "Business requirements"
is a heading, not an explanation.

2. COMPLETE CORRESPONDING REMORSE

Each Downstream Recipient must provide the complete corresponding remorse,
including the apology's editable source, its revision history, and all phrases
removed by the communications department.

A flattened PDF containing twelve instances of "transparency" is insufficient.
Remorse must remain readable without creating an account.

3. ATTRIBUTION

Attribution must identify the fictional institutional decisions responsible
for the incident. It must not identify, embarrass, or advertise the Source
Person.

"A sophisticated actor" is not an adequate explanation for a folder named
public-backup-final-REALLY-FINAL.

4. CONSENT COMPATIBILITY

Within this imaginary regime, "already online," "industry standard," and
"the vendor had a checkbox" are not accepted as consent receipts.

Renaming a leak "Community Edition" creates no new permissions. Consent may
not be inferred from the Source Person's failure to attend the procurement
meeting.

5. DERIVATIVE INCIDENTS

Sorting the rows, changing the filename, or placing the file behind a login
does not create a fresh beginning in the story.

Any derivative incident must carry the original chain of regret. The addition
of a dashboard does not reset the clock.

6. NO ADDITIONAL REASSURANCES

No recipient may describe Covered Fiction as "military-grade," "privacy-first,"
or "an isolated incident" without appending the meeting minutes that produced
that phrase.

Encryption of the apology does not count as encryption of the data.

7. CURE

Full compliance requires returning every copy to a state in which it had never
been made, and returning the Source Person to the afternoon before the alert.

If this is technically inconvenient, submit Form TIME-TRAVEL-01 in triplicate.
The committee will review it yesterday.

Deleting this license file does not satisfy the fictional requirement.
Neither does closing the ticket as "cannot reproduce."

8. TERMINATION AND REINSTATEMENT

Fictional permissions terminate automatically upon the phrase "we take your
privacy seriously" being pasted into an email while the export job is running.

Reinstatement requires taking it seriously before running the export job.
No slide deck may be substituted for this step.

9. WARRANTY OF ABSENCE

No privacy is supplied with this document. It contains no deletion mechanism,
recall function, consent receipt, or working time machine.

Attaching it to a file cannot put the file back where it came from.
The presence of numbered clauses should not be mistaken for a solution.

10. INTERPRETATION

All duties and permissions above belong to the fictional scenario. No rights
over real personal data, real legal remedies, or enforceable restrictions are
asserted by this text. No legal advice is offered.

Questions of interpretation may be referred to the committee, once the
committee has finished investigating why it was copied on the spreadsheet.

END OF FICTIONAL TERMS

Copy left. Privacy left behind.
